#### § 299.1 Purpose and scope.

This part prescribes minimum Federal safety standards for the high-speed transportation system described in detail in [§ 299.13](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-49/section-299.13), known as Texas Central Railroad, LLC and hereinafter referred to as the “railroad.” The purpose of this part is to prevent accidents, casualties, and property damage which could result from operation of this system.

#### § 299.3 Applicability.

(a) This part applies only to the railroad, as described in [§ 299.13](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-49/section-299.13).

(b) Except as stated in [paragraph (c)](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-49/section-299.3#p-299.3(c)) of this section, this part, rather than the generally applicable Federal railroad safety regulations, shall apply to the railroad.

(c) The following Federal railroad safety regulations found in [Title 49 of the Code of Federal Regulations](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-49), and any amendments are applicable to the railroad.

(1) Part 207, Railroad Police Officers;

(2) Part 209, Railroad Safety Enforcement Procedures;

(3) Part 210, Railroad Noise Emission Compliance Regulations;

(4) Part 211, Rules of Practice;

(5) Part 212, State Safety Participation Regulations;

(6) Part 214, Railroad Workplace Safety, except [§ 214.339](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-49/section-214.339);

(7) Part 216, Special Notice and Emergency Order Procedures;

(8) Part 218, Railroad Operating Practices;

(9) Part 219, Control of Alcohol and Drug Use;

(10) Part 220, Radio Standards and Procedures;

(11) Part 225, Railroad Accidents/Incidents: Reports, Classification, and Investigations;

